    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. that makes sense. one more thing though, what kind of minimum insurance coverage is required under CIF? i've heard there are different levels for different types of cargo, so i want to make sure our shipment is actually protected properly. is there a specific standard they have to meet?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The CIF term itself doesn't dictate a specific minimum percentage of insurance coverage, which is a common point of confusion. It generally requires the seller to provide insurance coverage that covers at least the CIF value (Cost, Insurance, and Freight) of the goods. However, for electronics, which are often delicate, you should absolutely ensure the insurance covers \"All Risks\" rather than just basic coverage. It's best to check the specific insurance policy documentation to confirm the level of coverage matches the value of your shipment.",
      "source": "target",
